//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Intersection of Two Linked Lists (Common Values)

Given two linked lists head1 and head2, find the intersection based on common node VALUES. Each list contains distinct node values.

Return a new linked list containing common values in the order they appear in head1. Return null if no common elements exist.

Examples:

Input:  List1: 9 -> 6 -> 4 -> 2 -> 3 -> 8
        List2: 1 -> 2 -> 8 -> 6
Output: 6 -> 2 -> 8

Input:  List1: 5 -> 3 -> 1 -> 13 -> 14
        List2: 3 -> 13
Output: 3 -> 13

Constraints:
- 1 <= no. of nodes <= 10^4
- 1 <= node->data <= 10^5

Time Complexity: O(m + n) ✓
Space Complexity: O(m + n) ✓


Time: O(m + n)  |  Space: O(m + n)
